{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>As they journeyed</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: <b>as they journeyed from the camp</b> (Numbers 10:17). This is what the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: \"That day they turned away from after YHWH\" — like a child who flees from the scroll. That is, <b>as they journeyed</b> means that they journeyed from the Ancient One of the world."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The phrase 'מקדמונו של עולם' is read as 'from the One who preceded the world,' i.e., YHWH; the wordplay turns 'מקדם' (eastward/forward) into 'from the Ancient One.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:55.773598317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}